<%- include('../partials/head', { title: 'Lead Intake' }) %>
<%- include('../partials/nav') %>
<div class="container" style="max-width: 820px;">
  <p class="mb-1"><a href="<%= basePath %>/admin/settings">&larr; Settings</a></p>
  <h1 class="h3 mb-1">Lead intake</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">Send enquiries from your website straight into <a href="<%= basePath %>/admin/leads">Leads</a>, so nobody re-types them.</p>

  <% if (rotated) { %>
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
      New key generated. The old one stopped working immediately &mdash; update your website
      before your next enquiry, or it will be rejected.
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">Your endpoint</h2>
      <p class="text-muted small">Your website posts JSON here. Every request must carry your key in the <code>X-CHO-Hub-Secret</code> header &mdash; that header is how we know the lead is yours.</p>

      <label class="form-label mb-1">Endpoint URL</label>
      <input class="form-control mb-3" readonly value="<%= endpoint %>">

      <label class="form-label mb-1">Your key</label>
      <% if (org.lead_webhook_secret) { %>
        <input class="form-control font-monospace mb-2" readonly value="<%= org.lead_webhook_secret %>">
        <p class="text-muted small">Treat this like a password &mdash; anyone holding it can create leads in your account.</p>
        <form method="POST" action="<%= basePath %>/admin/settings/lead-intake/rotate">
          <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" type="submit">Generate a new key</button>
          <span class="text-muted small ms-2">Use this if the key has been shared or exposed.</span>
        </form>
      <% } else { %>
        <p class="text-muted">No key yet.</p>
        <form method="POST" action="<%= basePath %>/admin/settings/lead-intake/rotate">
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Generate a key</button>
        </form>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">What to send</h2>
      <p class="text-muted small">Only <code>name</code> and <code>email</code> are required. Send whichever of the rest your form collects; anything else you include is kept on the lead as raw data, so nothing a customer typed is lost even if there's no field for it yet.</p>
      <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-sm">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td class="text-muted small">Required.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>email</code></td><td class="text-muted small">Required.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>phone</code></td><td class="text-muted small"></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>property_address</code></td><td class="text-muted small">Where the work would happen.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>interests</code></td><td class="text-muted small">A list, e.g. <code>["Lawn care","Irrigation"]</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>budget</code>, <code>timeline</code></td><td class="text-muted small">Free text, exactly as the customer chose it.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>additional_details</code></td><td class="text-muted small">Their &ldquo;anything else?&rdquo; box.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5">Wiring it up</h2>
      <p class="text-muted small mb-3">Any website that can send a webhook will work &mdash; the endpoint takes plain JSON, so it isn't tied to one platform.</p>

      <h3 class="h6 mb-1">WordPress</h3>
      <p class="text-muted small">Most form plugins (Elementor Pro, WPForms, Gravity Forms, Contact&nbsp;Form&nbsp;7) can post to a URL on submit &mdash; look for &ldquo;Webhook&rdquo; in the form's actions. Set the URL above, add the header, and map your fields to the names in the table.</p>

      <h3 class="h6 mb-1 mt-3">Squarespace, Wix, Webflow, HubSpot</h3>
      <p class="text-muted small">Use the platform's webhook or automation step, or connect it through Zapier / Make. Same URL, same header.</p>

      <h3 class="h6 mb-1 mt-3">Anything else</h3>
      <p class="text-muted small mb-2">If your site can't send webhooks, your web developer can post from the form handler directly:</p>
      <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded small mb-0"><code>POST <%= endpoint %>
Content-Type: application/json
X-CHO-Hub-Secret: <%= org.lead_webhook_secret || 'your-key-here' %>

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "phone": "555-0100",
  "property_address": "12 Oak Street",
  "interests": ["Lawn care"],
  "additional_details": "Quarter-acre lot, weekly in summer"
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-muted small">
    Leads arriving here land in <a href="<%= basePath %>/admin/leads">Leads</a>, where you
    can work them and convert one into a customer.
  </p>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
